      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks! I like this optimization and makes the device coordinate system consistent with a few other places that also just derive the inverse from the available component matrices instead of calling SkM44::invert().\n\nThe code looks correct to me, and the skia diffs are negligible and don\u0027t suggest any bugs that we overlooked. However, running the Canary-Chromium bot shows that we have layout test failures that will block rolling into chromium. I have a comment below that outlines how we can move forward.\n\nLooking at the layout test failures, filters-color-01-b.svg, nested-reflection-on-overflow.html, and nested-reflection.html all look imperceptible and what I\u0027d expect from slight changes to matrix calculations. The colrv1-samples-visual.html diffs are more troubling but I am not sure if this is related to your CL or something else that changed in skia or chromium that was included in the canary bot.\n\nI\u0027ve rebased and re-run the try job to see if it reproduces. I would not expect colrv1 text rendering to be dependent on how the device-to-global inverse is calculated, so fingers crossed those failures don\u0027t repeat.",
      "revId": "c5decf009bdfb223c52dc79b3313cd906e0c3cc3",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bcf4a13e_253e2b65",
        "filename": "src/core/SkCanvas.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
